<header class="page-head">
  <p class="eyebrow">Writing</p>
  <h1>About the archive</h1>
  <p class="lede">This site is meant to become a complete record of Wayne Martin Mellinger’s writing. Every work is one record, described in four separate ways.</p>
</header>
<div class="prose">
  <h2>Four ways to find a work</h2>
  <dl class="defs">
    <dt>Collection</dt>
    <dd>Where it appeared: Noozhawk, a journal or book, one of Wayne’s research platforms, or <cite>Moments of Awe</cite>. This is a fact about the work.</dd>
    <dt>Kind</dt>
    <dd>What sort of thing it is: a column, essay, article, chapter, book or poem. Also a fact.</dd>
    <dt>Body of work</dt>
    <dd>The larger intellectual project a work substantively contributes to, such as Critical Interactionism or Religious &amp; Dionysian Naturalism. This is a judgment, not a fact, and many works belong to none — a column can be good public writing without advancing a research program.</dd>
    <dt>Topic</dt>
    <dd>What a work discusses: homelessness, mental health, Santa Barbara history and so on. Also a judgment. So far only the Noozhawk columns carry topics.</dd>
  </dl>

  <h2>What “provisional” means</h2>
  <p>Bodies of work and topics were assigned in a first pass, some from reading the full text, some from titles, and some from Wayne’s own groupings on his earlier site. None has yet been reviewed by Wayne. Until they are, the site calls them provisional, and they may change. Titles, dates, places of publication and links are recorded as published and are not changed to fit the categories.</p>

  <h2>What is here, and what is not yet</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Noozhawk</strong> — every column, compiled from Noozhawk’s author archive on October 1, 2026.</li>
    <li><strong>Scholarly publications</strong> — the peer-reviewed list from the earlier site; citations still to be checked against the journals.</li>
    <li><strong>Doing Modernity, The Dionysian Naturalist, Wild Flesh</strong> — the works Wayne listed on the earlier site, with his annotations. Each platform holds more than is catalogued here.</li>
    <li><strong>Poems</strong> — the selection from <cite>Moments of Awe Punctuated by the Mundane</cite> shown on the earlier site.</li>
    <li><strong>Not yet catalogued</strong> — Our Neighbors on the Streets, writing for other publications, and the full archives of the three research platforms.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>Where a date was not given, it is taken from the original web address and noted in the record, or left undated. Nothing is dated by guesswork.</p>

  <h2>Corrections</h2>
  <p>Found a wrong date, a broken link or a missing piece? <a href="/contact/">Please write.</a></p>
</div>
